{"id": "20542144", "revid": "15881234", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20542144", "title": "Wageningse Berg", "text": "The Wageningse Berg () is the southernmost part of the Veluwe, a range of hills that originated as a glacial moraine. It lies just north of the Nederrijn and to the east of the town of Wageningen and has an elevation of 42 m above mean sea level (NAP).\nIt is also the name of a football stadium home to the football club FC Wageningen, defunct since 1992. Since 2024 the stadium is in use again as a football team training camp ground."}
