{"id": "20544007", "revid": "753665", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20544007", "title": "Jean-Claude Olry", "text": "Jean-Claude Patrice Jacques Bernard Olry (born 28 December 1949 in Boves, Somme) is a French retired slalom canoeist who competed in the late 1960s and early 1970s. He won a bronze in the C-2 event at the 1972 Summer Olympics in Munich.\nOlry also won two medals at the 1969 ICF Canoe Slalom World Championships in Bourg St.-Maurice with a gold in the C-2 event and a bronze in the C-2 team event.\nHe won all his medals while partnering his brother Jean-Louis."}
