{"id": "20544526", "revid": "24465790", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20544526", "title": "Sebacinaceae", "text": "The Sebacinaceae are a family of fungi in the order Sebacinales. Species produce basidiocarps (fruit bodies} that are gelatinous or cartilaginous and variously corticioid, clavarioid, bracket-like, or jelly-like. Microscopically, all have septate basidia and hyphae lacking clamp connections. Many but not all species are mycorrhizal, forming associations with a wide range of plants."}
