{"id": "20544782", "revid": "15482012", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20544782", "title": "Behind the Cow", "text": "\"Behind the Cow\" is a song by German band Scooter featuring American hip hop artist Fatman Scoop. Premiered at \"The Dome 40\" in D\u00fcsseldorf on 1 December 2006, it was released on 19 January 2007 as the lead single from Scooter's twelfth studio album \"The Ultimate Aural Orgasm\". Jeff \"Mantas\" Dunn plays guitar on the track. \"Behind the Cow\" samples music and lyrics from the KLF song \"What Time Is Love?\" and music from Blue \u00d6yster Cult song \"(Don't Fear) The Reaper\".\nMusic video.\nThe video was filmed in India, where the band caused controversy by painting a cow, an animal considered holy in India.\nTrack listing.\nCD single &amp; Download\n12-inch"}
