{"id": "20545057", "revid": "45669981", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20545057", "title": "John Harryson", "text": "John Edvard Harryson (17 April 1926 \u2013 28 November 2008) was a Swedish actor. He was the father of famous Swedish actor and television host Peter Harryson.\nBorn in Katrineholm, Harrysson was a renowned actor in Sweden. For a younger generation John Harrysson was known as the Swedish voice of Scrooge McDuck, Eeyore in Winnie the Pooh, Doctor Snuggles, Bert in Svenska Sesam (The second Swedish version of Sesame Street), and the Sheriff of Nottingham in \"Robin Hood\" (1973).\nHe was also active as a folk singer and has recorded several albums over the years, including \"Bondkomikernas viser\" 1971, Birger Sj\u00f6bergs \"Fridas viser\" 1978 and poems set to music by Eino Leino 1981. John Harryson is buried in the memorial garden at Kungsholms cemetery. "}
