{"id": "20545124", "revid": "51034171", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20545124", "title": "Littleferry", "text": "Littleferry () is a village on the north east shore of Loch Fleet in Golspie, Sutherland, and is in the Scottish council area of Highland. \nLittleferry lies at the entrance to Loch Fleet, 3 miles (5\u00a0km) southwest of Golspie. Its name is derived from the ferry that once crossed the narrow channel here. \nThe Battle of Littleferry was a skirmish between a Jacobite force of the George Mackenzie, 3rd Earl of Cromartie and government troops under Ensign John Mackay of Golspie on the eve of the Battle of Culloden in 1746."}
